Subject: [PATCH 0067] nmxtrace=3 writes NVRAM only for NMXGPU's own steps; steps inside NMXGPUFB::start

Wildcat Lake test start 11 (with 0066): the scan-out buffer mapped (vmap 0), the panel modeset succeeded
("modeset commit (err) 0", vblanks at 16.6 ms, no FIFO underruns), drm_client_register's re-commit ran, and the start
froze after "publish: IOFramebuffer start". In the log every checkpoint cost ~15 ms (its NVRAM write) and one cost
3.7 s while the whole Mac went silent and USB threads reported being stuck >1 s: the firmware compacting its NVRAM
flash store, filled by hundreds of breadcrumb writes per start once the modeset path had checkpoints (0062).

- bsdcompat/src/nmx_trace.c: nmxtrace=3 still prints every checkpoint but writes the NVRAM breadcrumb only for steps
  named attach:, publish: or fb: (~25 per start).
- xnu/nmx_fb.cpp: publish: steps around IOFramebuffer::start, the vblank timer and registerPowerDriver in
  NMXGPUFB::start (the nmx_trace declaration moves to the top of the file).

Applies on top of 0051-0066.

diff --git a/gpu-port/xkpi/bsdcompat/src/nmx_trace.c b/gpu-port/xkpi/bsdcompat/src/nmx_trace.c
--- a/gpu-port/xkpi/bsdcompat/src/nmx_trace.c
+++ b/gpu-port/xkpi/bsdcompat/src/nmx_trace.c
@@ -3,8 +3,11 @@
  * the attach before xe printed a line, and nothing reached the log). Off unless asked for at boot:
  *   nmxtrace=1         prints "NMXT <step>" on the console before each step of the attach and of xe's probe
  *   nmxtrace=2         the same, then waits 200 ms so the line is on screen before a step that hangs
- *   nmxtrace=3         prints each step and keeps the last one in NVRAM (nullmoth-gpu-trace, synced), for a hang
- *                      that blanks the screen: read it at the next start with  nvram nullmoth-gpu-trace
+ *   nmxtrace=3         prints each step and keeps the last NMXGPU step (attach:, publish:, fb:) in NVRAM
+ *                      (nullmoth-gpu-trace, synced), for a hang that blanks the screen: read it at the next start
+ *                      with  nvram nullmoth-gpu-trace. Only those ~25 steps: every NVRAM write appends to the
+ *                      firmware's flash store, and hundreds per start (all of xe's and the display's checkpoints)
+ *                      filled it until the firmware compacted it, stalling the whole Mac for seconds (test 11).
  *   nmxdrmdebug=<mask> sets drm.debug (DRM_UT_* bits; 0x106 = driver, KMS, DP) for this start
  * The steps are marked in xnu/nmx_kext.cpp, bsdcompat/src/nmx_port.c and (by fork_xe.py) xe's probe functions.
  */
@@ -46,7 +49,8 @@
     printf("NMXT %s %ld\n", what, val);
     if (nmx_trace_level == 2)
         IOSleep(200);
-    if (nmx_trace_level >= 3) {
+    if (nmx_trace_level >= 3 && (strncmp(what, "attach:", 7) == 0 || strncmp(what, "publish:", 8) == 0 ||
+                                 strncmp(what, "fb:", 3) == 0)) {
         char crumb[128];
 
         snprintf(crumb, sizeof(crumb), "%s %ld", what, val);
